    <p class="callout__eyebrow">The usual bad advice</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>Pick the career with the biggest number and everything will work out.</li>
      <li>High salary means the same thing at 22, 30, and 40.</li>
      <li>Only doctor or engineer careers really count as high-pay options.</li>
      <li>If the title sounds prestigious, the money will follow automatically.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      None of that tells you what creates the pay, how long it takes, what work you will do daily, or whether the path actually fits you.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Salary matters.
  </p>

  <p>
    But the pay engine matters more.
  </p>

